WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
A hardcoded model name

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.000
is right exactly once.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.492
This picks the model for you,

00:00:07.492 --> 00:00:10.500
so your code never has to know one.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.575
The name you typed was true on one laptop,

00:00:12.575 --> 00:00:14.305
on one afternoon. It outlives both.

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:15.441
Nothing re-decides when

00:00:15.441 --> 00:00:16.479
the hardware changes.

00:00:16.479 --> 00:00:17.863
Nothing tells you it stopped

00:00:17.863 --> 00:00:19.000
being the right answer.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.445
So describe the job instead.

00:00:20.445 --> 00:00:22.303
It reads the machine in front of it,

00:00:22.303 --> 00:00:23.851
ranks only what actually fits,

00:00:23.851 --> 00:00:25.503
then writes the answer to a file

00:00:25.503 --> 00:00:27.000
your code reads at call time.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.047
Here is the part that is not obvious.

00:00:28.047 --> 00:00:28.867
It measures the speed instead

00:00:28.867 --> 00:00:29.292
of assuming it.

00:00:29.292 --> 00:00:30.056
An estimate of twenty-eight

00:00:30.056 --> 00:00:30.622
point three tokens a

00:00:30.622 --> 00:00:31.443
second sails past the comfort

00:00:31.443 --> 00:00:31.924
floor of fifteen.

00:00:31.924 --> 00:00:32.915
The measurement, fifteen point two,

00:00:32.915 --> 00:00:33.481
only just clears it.

00:00:33.481 --> 00:00:34.216
That gap is the difference

00:00:34.216 --> 00:00:34.896
between a recommendation

00:00:34.896 --> 00:00:35.547
that sounds comfortable

00:00:35.547 --> 00:00:36.000
and one that is.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.459
Any OpenAI SDK, unchanged.

00:00:38.459 --> 00:00:40.918
Ask for model equals best.

00:00:40.918 --> 00:00:43.000
The right one answers.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.237
It is at deraison dot a i

00:00:44.237 --> 00:00:45.475
slash a i hyphen helpers.

00:00:45.475 --> 00:00:46.712
Leave a star on GitHub if

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:48.000
it saved you an afternoon.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Name the job. Never the model.
